  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations to New Jersey totaled $6.2B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $4.1B, accounting for the bulk of that total. Award activity included 321,445 awards with an average award size of $19.4K. Obligations fell 33.3% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show prior totals of $8.9B in FY21, $9.3B in FY22, $9.2B in FY23, $9.8B in FY24, and $9.3B in FY25. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION received $1.7B, making that firm the largest vendor by dollars in FY2026 to date. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry by obligation with $1.3B, followed by Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $786M. Other notable buyers include the Department of Veterans Affairs at $607M and the Department of Homeland Security at $577M. This snapshot reflects partial fiscal-year totals and shows where federal buying concentrated in New Jersey so far in FY2026.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the biggest buyers in New Jersey?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $4.1B in obligations. The Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $607M, and the Department of Homeland Security follows with $577M. Other significant buyers include the Department of Transportation at $264M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $172M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who wins the largest awards and which industries dominate?",
        "body": "LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION is the top vendor with $1.7B in obligations. ASRC FEDERAL FACILITIES LOGISTICS, LLC follows with $443M and WHITING-TURNER CONTRACTING COMPANY, THE follows with $400M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences leads industries with $1.3B, and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing follows with $786M."
      }
